# Holos content guardrails

The site content is the source of truth for the framework's positions: `Logic.tsx` for commitments, `Predictions.tsx` for tests and speculation. The history of each change, and why it was made, is in `wiki/log.md`. Read the relevant section before editing it.

## Retired claims: do not reintroduce

- **Ordered dark matter** and everything built on it: Succession Nodes, the IDE-Pivot equation and "Succession Operator", dark energy as "fuel", DESI weakening as a signature of Succession, JWST COSMOS-Web mass peaks as nodes, axion-like particles as a substrate for "migration into the Bulk". Cosmological dark matter predates life (the CMB shows it) and outweighs all the ordinary matter anything could be built from. Dark Nodes are ordinary matter that has stopped shining: a trace population, a search channel and not a fingerprint.
- **Observation as selection, or as a constraint on earlier states.** Observation selects nothing, erases nothing, and changes no physics. Experience is lived inside observers; their causal pasts are lit; the rest remains unlit structure. Records are definite within each branch without observers (a detector's click included); an observer adds not definiteness but its being lived.
- **Born weights as shares of experience.** The weights are structural facts within C. For an observer they are self-locating odds: after a split and before looking, a branch's weight is your odds of being among its observers.
- **Branch counting as a measure.** Branches and observers cannot be counted; counting gives an arbitrary or infinite number. Weight is the only measure that survives subdivision.
- **Theological and secular readings as interchangeable.** The monist reading is the framework's position.
- **"Falsified outright" for the standing bet.** A consciousness-linked collapse would falsify Axiom 2's no-collapse reading, branching with self-locating odds, and the claim that observation changes nothing it registers. Axiom 4 survives: experience adds no force beyond the physics, which would then include a collapse law; never list Axiom 4 among the losses. The declared fallback keeps the core: the threshold becomes the collapse point (a Chalmers and McQueen style reading), Omega is the universe with one history, and lived, lit, and unlit apply within it. Integration-tied collapse would be the strongest confirmation the threshold could get; size-tied (objective) collapse would falsify Axiom 2 with nothing gained, the threshold staying inert. The core loses only through Test A.
- **"Confirmed so far" for the standing bet.** No superposition tested so far has contained an observer. The bet is untested.
- **Omega as the ground of record agreement.** Physics secures agreement: the same signals reach observers who meet. Omega's one job is unity: every observer is the one subject, so crossing the threshold adds a place where it wakes, not a new self. Omega does not explain where waking happens; the threshold does, on any picture. Its payoff is economy (one subject instead of billions arising without explanation), and it is philosophical, not experimental. Do not claim Omega explains why there is experience at all; the posits take experience as given.
- **The qubit observer-cut experiment.** Qubits register nothing below the threshold. Check B is a consistency check, not a test.

## Current commitments in brief

- Omega is physically the universe's complete quantum state: all branches included on the no-collapse reading (Axiom 2), a single history on a collapse reading. Never define Omega through Axiom 2, or the claim that Axioms 1, 3, 4, and 5 hold on any reading fails. Its existence rests on physics on any reading; what Holos adds is only that this whole is the one experiencer, which is interpretive and untestable. The title says "Bounded by Physics"; do not switch to "Grounded in Physics" until the threshold is measured.
- Five axioms make the framework: 1 Relationality, 2 Conservation (unitary, no collapse), 3 Threshold, 4 Two Sides, 5 Totality. Axioms 3 and 5 are the two additions to physics. The core is Axioms 1, 3, 4, and 5, which hold under any reading of quantum physics; Axiom 2 is the side taken on quantum physics and carries the declared fallback. Never call all five "the core". Commitments 1 and 2 are fundamental; Commitment 3 rests on Axiom 2. Every Proposition and Commitment names the axioms it follows from; Proposition IV (infinities) is a principle of method. Structural Constraint is a companion principle, not an axiom. Lived, lit, and unlit are definitions (D7).
- Two additions to physics: the integration threshold Φ_c, and the totality Omega as the one experiencer.
- Physics side: unitary, no collapse, branching. Relational QM is borrowed only for indexing registered facts to observers, not adopted.
- Observer requirements number four: integration (which includes feedback: parts constrain one another in both directions over time; never list recursion or causal autonomy separately), differentiation, temporal cohesion, and aboutness (the variety the system can take on must be variety the world can drive through input channels of its own, across much of its range: the piano, not the one-button jukebox; channels may be open or temporarily gated, so dreams pass; any channel counts, including text; the requirement judges the machine, not the message, so a brain in a vat and Helen Keller qualify). Never phrase aboutness as tracking the world "as it happens" (excludes dreams) or as merely having a live channel (one wired sensor would rescue an inert array). Aboutness is structural, not historical, so "no dark duplicates" holds. It is what rules out high-Φ logic-gate arrays (Aaronson's objection), wired or not.
- Axiom 4 (Two Sides) is dual-aspect: in an observer, experience and physical activity are two sides of one event. No dark duplicates holds in any possible world. Experience adds no force but is causally efficacious as the inside of physical causation; never describe it as a byproduct or as along for the ride.
- Incompleteness is in the description, not the world: physics fixes every fact but states it only from outside, and cannot say that any of it is lived. Never say physics misses a fact or that something exists beyond what it fixes; that would contradict no dark duplicates. The floor-plan example is the canonical gloss.
- AI: integration is measured where a system's causes are organized, whatever it is made of. For current text-only AI, observerhood is an open question with one border: integration. Aboutness is met narrowly (the conversation). Never say it lacks a world because its input is text. Do not say "no one home", and do not claim current AI is conscious. Fluency is never evidence either way.
- ⊛ is ordinary composition: R = O(C(S)), "possibility, then registration", an order of logic, not time. Nothing exotic is claimed for the glyph. Never say C and O "constrain each other", "remain coupled", or form a feedback loop (not even "the loop between creation and observation"), and never call observation a process in time; registration changes nothing it registers. R is the family of lived perspectives, one per observer per branch, each with the lit world it draws on. Iteration only follows one observer's thread. The buffet gloss: every dish is really there, cooked from the recipes (the laws); tasting happens only where someone eats, and tasting never changes a dish. Do not use the cookbook gloss (it makes unlived branches look like uncooked recipes, i.e. unreal). Creation is what physics actually produces from the universe's state, every branch of the one quantum state; never define it as every world the laws permit or say "every possibility remains". Worlds the laws merely allow from other beginnings are possibilities, not structure, and are not part of Omega. "Possibility" stays acceptable as the view from inside one branch: the others are its possibilities, and all of them occur.
- "Real" has two strengths: structure is real whether or not it is lived; R is structure that is also lived. Use "lived" for where experience occurs, "lit" for observers' causal pasts, and "unlit" for the rest.
- Three words, one meaning each. **Lived**: where experience occurs, inside apertures only; no one lived through the early universe. **Lit**: binary, the causal past of at least one aperture in its branch, the world experience is made from and about ("an aperture lights its past"). **Unlit**: outside every aperture's causal past (observer-free branches, beyond every horizon). **Witnessing**: graded, how much of the lit region experience is actually about. The old term "sealing" is retired in favor of "lit"; never say a region outside an aperture is "lived". Do not reintroduce branch-wide lighting "from beginning to end". Apertures cut off from one another are "walled off".

## Style

- Plain language for a general reader; gloss technical terms on first use.
- No em dashes; use colons, commas, or periods.
- **Economy as Omega's payoff.** "One subject instead of billions" is only a count; both pictures leave where and what to the threshold. Omega's stated work is dissolving "why am I this one?" (the vertiginous question) and the duplication puzzle (Parfit). Name the view open individualism (Kolak). Never claim Omega explains where or what experience is.
- **"Fundamental" experience.** Means underived (the fact Holos starts from), never "everywhere" or "free of physics". Proposition I and Axiom 1 do not reach experience.
- **Threshold strength.** The threshold is four claims of different strength (Logic `#threshold-claims`): (1) Edge: clear cases on both sides and a narrow twilight between, where there is no exact fact; part of Axiom 3. (2) Integration: integration plus the other requirements carries a system across; the core claim, lost only through Test A. (3) Transition: the crossing is a critical transition; hypothesis. (4) Shape: every crossing shares one universality class; boldest hypothesis, with the twilight narrowing by one finite-size-scaling rule as its test. Boldest version: one universal Φ_c under a size-independent measure, a structural constant like a percolation threshold. If 3 or 4 fail, the core stands and the twilight is wider. Never say presence is binary, that there is "no halfway state", or that an exact line exists in a finite system: exact lines exist only in infinite systems, which Proposition IV reads as model limits. Never call "graded presence" a way to lose. Where the twilight falls is fixed by structure in every possible world, so a copy of a borderline system is borderline too; never call the threshold a contingent constant of nature "like the speed of light". Holos rejects the no-vagueness premise (Antony) with Schwitzgebel's reply; clear cases stay clear, so the twilight is not panpsychism. Integration is the result, not the knob: conditions (wiring, development, drug level) move it; Φ ≥ Φ_c is shorthand for past the twilight. Near-criticality of waking cortex (Toker 2022, avalanches, the 2024 EEG study) marks the operating point, where differentiation and richness peak, not the threshold; never cite it as evidence for claims 3 or 4. Seizures are joined but not varied (differentiation fails); psychedelics move cortex closer to criticality. Toker studied waking, generalized seizure, anesthesia, psychedelics, and disorders of consciousness, not deep sleep. Neural inertia (hysteresis) fits claim 3 as a first-order switch and counts against claim 4; never cite it for claim 4. Do not use water freezing as the threshold analogy; use the Curie point.
- **Unlit examples.** Use aperture-free branches and regions beyond every observer's horizon. Never cite "the far future after the last observer": fluctuation observers (Boltzmann brains) in some branch could light it.
- **Born odds under monism.** Self-locating uncertainty belongs to each walled-off aperture, not to Omega. Keep "why am I this one?" (a reason, dissolved by monism) apart from "which one is this?" (information, answered by the Born odds).
- **Describing language models.** Information flows up through layers and forward in time at each level via stored notes (the KV cache) that later steps read but never rewrite; the only top-to-bottom path is the output word. Never say the loop is "only one word wide".
- **Star-level waste heat.** The Integration Hypothesis points to single stars warm in the infrared, not galaxies. As of 2026-09-26 the Hephaistos candidates are mostly traced or suspected to be background galaxies; never present them as live technosignatures.
- **Omega is not a limit.** Omega is the whole, existing now: physically the universal quantum state, experientially the one experiencer. Never call it a limit, endpoint, or horizon finite systems approach, and never say it is fully registered or fully integrated ("nothing unregistered"): unlit structure is part of it and never lived. Say "Omega", not "the Omega Point", except when naming Teilhard or Tipler. Omega is the ultimate whole, not the ultimate integration: everything is in it, all at once, but its parts are not all joined. Never exempt Omega from maximality as "not a system among systems" or a "category mistake"; the reason it is never a peak is physical: the whole splits into parts that never touch (regions beyond each other's horizons, decohered branches), so its integration is near zero. This also explains why it pools nothing. Its Logic material lives in the core section `#totality`; `#extrapolative-proposition` holds only the Structural Constraint companion principle.
- **Speculation standard.** Every item in Speculation must be physically possible, not extremely unlikely, and carry a "Why it is plausible" note grounded in known physics or published work. Modify or remove anything that fails. Never restate the Teeming Dark or Aliens there; point to them.
